Z||000004||1FST2M6||02-23-2001||04:59 PM||||HEH i know.. i can't drive worth the crap! the car always seemed to make up for it though.. well straight anyway.. it wasn't very forgiving in the corners... too much gas and POOF i'm a dust cloud in everyone elses mirrors! maybe the automatic will help that.. can't wait till april when the tracks open back up!  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||BBBAD GT||02-23-2001||06:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mshill:<BR><B>1FST2M6,  just think what your time would have been on that slip if you had the Mustang drivers reaction time   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Reaction time isn't considered in the ET.  The timing starts when you break both beams, how long it takes you to cross both beams from when the light turns green is reaction time.  Reaction time comes into play as to who's first at the finish line.  You can be first at the line, but have a slower ET.  <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">      <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT (sold)</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||JBGehling||02-23-2001||10:03 PM||||Aw c'mon! No stock Fiero ever did 0-60 in 6.9 seconds! Where did you get those stats, I'd be genuinly suprised if a stock V-6 Fiero was running 7.5 in 0-60. I mean, I love these cars to death, but they're times just aren't THAT good.<P>Josh||||reg||1
